---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/prose.css';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ali Alp Özer: AI engineer in Munich, three languages deep, reskilling from enterprise software into applied AI."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h1>I am an engineer who keeps starting over, on purpose.</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am Ali Alp Özer. I build AI systems in Munich: retrieval pipelines, autonomous
        agents, and the evaluation harnesses that decide whether either of those is working.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before that I spent three years at Flexus AG in Würzburg building enterprise software
        in SAP CAP, on a product that won an international SAP Innovation Award. I owned the
        backend architecture, the fleet management cockpit, and eventually the roadmap for
        it. It was a good job and I learned the thing that most AI content skips entirely:
        what it takes for software to survive in front of people who did not choose it and
        cannot work around it.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I left a good job to start again</h2>

      <p>
        Because I could see which half of my skills was going to matter in ten years, and it
        was not the half I was being paid for.
      </p>

      <p>
        So in June 2026 I put myself through a sixteen-week program of my own design: LLM
        applications, retrieval, agents, evaluation, fine-tuning. Not a course with a
        certificate at the end. A syllabus where every block has to end in a repository that
        runs. That constraint is why <a href="/work/sage">Sage</a> has a hand-labelled golden
        set instead of a demo, and why the
        <a href="/work/munich-apartment-agent">Munich Apartment Agent</a> has durable
        checkpointing instead of a screenshot.
      </p>

      <h2>What I actually care about</h2>

      <p>
        The unglamorous half. Anyone can get a language model to produce something impressive
        once. The engineering is in the second time, and the thousandth, when the input is
        malformed and the API is down and the model has quietly started making things up.
      </p>

      <p>
        That is why almost everything I build has an evaluation harness in it, usually one
        that took longer than the thing it measures. A system whose output you cannot check
        is not a system, it is a demo with good lighting.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        <p>Success is observed, not claimed. Exit code zero is necessary and not sufficient.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Three languages, three countries</h2>

      <p>
        I learned German at school in Turkey, arrived in Germany at B2, and reached C2 within
        a year. Then I completed an entire Bachelor's degree in it. English I learned properly
        during the preparation year at ODTÜ, where I had been admitted after placing in the
        top 0.15% nationally in the Turkish university entrance examination. Turkish is my
        first language.
      </p>

      <p>
        None of that was a straight line and I have stopped pretending it should have been.
        Changing university, changing country, changing field: each one cost time and each
        one is the reason I can do something now that I could not do before. The
        <a href="/journey">journey page</a> has the actual sequence if you want it.
      </p>

      <h2>Where this goes next</h2>

      <p>
        I start an MSc in Wirtschaftsinformatik at the Technical University of Munich this
        October, to push the formal side of what I have been teaching myself: the mathematics
        under the models rather than the APIs on top of them. Alongside it I am building
        <a href="/work/advocate">Advocate</a>, which is the most opinionated thing I have
        made, and continuing to write down what I learn.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you are hiring for AI engineering work, or you have something hard and
        badly-specified that needs building, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>write to me</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-lg); }
  .page-head .label { margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .prose { padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl); }
</style>
